Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:0073a376124f045d48fef89c5022bf16a2d6817795542c9761520aef9c699164","file":"preprints/The-entropy-rate-dimension-formula-for-self-similar-measures-on-the-line-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":78,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"7b139940d64078a175fc126a8df44c0f8c6665fa5f49d4f2f1260c8fd180bdf5","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/The-entropy-rate-dimension-formula-for-self-similar-measures-on-the-line-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:0073a376124f045d48fef89c5022bf16a2d6817795542c9761520aef9c699164","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-entropy-rate-dimension-formula-for-self-similar-measures-on-the-line-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L78"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nFor every finite nonempty indexed family\n$\\varphi_i(x)=r_i x+t_i$ on $\\R$ with $0<|r_i|<1$, and every\nstrictly positive probability vector $p$, its self-similar measure satisfies\n\\[\n \\dim_H\\mu_{\\Phi,p}\n =\\min\\left\\{1,\\frac{h_{\\mathrm{RW}}(\\Phi,p)}{\\chi(\\Phi,p)}\\right\\}.\n\\]\nNo separation assumption is required; exact overlaps and repeated\ngenerators are allowed."}
